[340.893392, "o", "pdftotext LLM/2402.06079v2.pdf - | grep -i -C 2 -E \"Beethoven|Mozart|Bach|Jazz\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[340.938793, "o", "allows the use of ODE solvers to compute the reverse process efficiently (Song et al., 2020a; Lu et al., 2022; Zhang &\r\nChen, 2023; Xia et al., 2023). In this work, we will follow\r\n"]
[340.939016, "o", "the denoising view of the diffusion model, and use a reparameterising trick found in Latent Diffusion Models (Rom\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbach\u001b[m\u001b[K et al., 2022). In this notation, the training process can\r\nalso be interpreted as training a noise predictor εθ :\r\n\u0002\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[K--\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n2023), but LDMs are preferred for their computational\r\nefficiency - this is due to the compaction and smoothness\r\nof the latent space (Rom\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbach\u001b[m\u001b[K et al., 2022). Current\r\nstate-of-the-art models are usually domain-specific and rely\r\non pre-trained language models to form latent embeddings\r\n"]
[340.970825, "o", "\u001b[36m\u001b[K--\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n4.1.1. VAE A RCHITECTURE\r\nThe choice of VAE architecture in LDMs is critical and\r\noften domain-specific. For example, Stable Diffusion (Rom\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbach\u001b[m\u001b[K et al., 2022) uses a hybrid architecture that combines\r\nconvolutional neural networks (CNNs) and 2d-attention for\r\nimage generation, while PLANNER (Zhang et al., 2023)\r\n"]
[341.021632, "o", "\u001b[36m\u001b[K--\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\narXiv:2301.12503, 2023.\r\n\r\nRom\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbach\u001b[m\u001b[K, R., Blattmann, A., Lorenz, D., Esser, P., and\r\nOmmer, B. High-resolution image synthesis with latent\r\ndiffusion models. In Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF\r\n"]
[341.049874, "o", "\u001b[36m\u001b[K--\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\nis equivalent to a special training schedule with the KL divergence term being fixed in the first stage, and then training\r\nthe denoising model in the second stage. The performance gain of separating the training process has been shown in the\r\nimage generation domain (Rom\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbach\u001b[m\u001b[K et al., 2022; Preechakul et al., 2022). In the section below, we provide the empirical\r\nevaluation of this method for DNA sequence generation.\r\n\r\nC. U-Net Configuration\r\nU-Net is trained by sampling t from uniform distribution U [1,T ] and ε from N (0,I). We adopted the U-Net backbone\r\nfrom LDM (Ho et al.; Liu et al., 2023; Ronneberger et al., 2015) to implement εθ (z t ,t). Cross-attention (Rom\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbach\u001b[m\u001b[K et al.,\r\n2022) is added to each layer to enable the integration of conditional information, and self-attention (Vaswani et al., 2017)\r\nis added to the middle layers to improve the expressive power of the network.\r\n"]
