[443.347137, "o", "--- LLM/2407.07093v1.pdf ---\r\n"]
[443.382128, "o", "FBI-LLM: Scaling Up Fully Binarized LLMs from"]
[443.382506, "o", "\r\n"]
[443.382716, "o", "Scratch via Autoregressive Distillation"]
[443.382889, "o", "\r\n"]
[443.383047, "o", "\r\n"]
[443.383222, "o", "Abstract"]
[443.383374, "o", "\r\n"]
[443.383558, "o", "This work presents a Fully BInarized Large Language Model (FBI-LLM), demonstrating for the first time how to train a large-scale binary language model from"]
[443.383711, "o", "\r\n"]
[443.383887, "o", "scratch (not the partial binary or ternary LLM like BitNet b1.58 [1]) to match the"]
[443.384051, "o", "\r\n"]
[443.384264, "o", "performance of its full-precision counterparts (e.g., FP16 or BF16) in transformerbased LLMs. It achieves this by employing an autoregressive distillation (AD) loss"]
[443.384431, "o", "\r\n"]
[443.384615, "o", "with maintaining equivalent model dimensions (130M, 1.3B, 7B) and training data"]
[443.384775, "o", "\r\n"]
[443.384951, "o", "volume as regular LLM pretraining, while delivering competitive results in terms"]
[443.385134, "o", "\r\n"]
[443.385284, "o", "of perplexity and task-specific effectiveness. Intriguingly, by analyzing the training"]
[443.385423, "o", "\r\n"]
[443.388931, "o", "--- LLM/2407.12036v2.pdf ---\r\n"]
[443.412171, "o", "E XPLORING A DVANCED L ARGE L ANGUAGE M ODELS WITH"]
